WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940
A strong monitoring strategy is risk-based.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.427
It does not treat every asset, alert, or metric as equally important.

3
00:00:07.427 --> 00:00:24.680
Critical systems, sensitive data, internet-facing services, privileged identities, regulated environments, mission-critical workflows, known weaknesses, and active threat exposure deserve more attention than low-impact systems with limited exposure.

4
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:29.941
Prioritization keeps monitoring from becoming a pile of disconnected signals.

5
00:00:29.941 --> 00:00:32.726
Start by defining monitoring objectives.

6
00:00:32.726 --> 00:00:35.588
What decisions should the program support?

7
00:00:35.588 --> 00:00:37.523
Detect unauthorized access?

8
00:00:37.523 --> 00:00:40.695
Identify vulnerable internet-facing systems?

9
00:00:40.695 --> 00:00:42.938
Prove controls remain operating?

10
00:00:42.938 --> 00:00:44.872
Track remediation progress?

11
00:00:44.872 --> 00:00:46.961
Watch for configuration drift?

12
00:00:46.961 --> 00:00:48.818
Support incident response?

13
00:00:48.818 --> 00:00:50.598
Maintain audit readiness?

14
00:00:50.598 --> 00:00:56.787
Different objectives require different signals, thresholds, owners, and escalation paths.

15
00:00:56.787 --> 00:01:01.274
Without clear objectives, teams often collect data that no one uses.

16
00:01:01.274 --> 00:01:03.518
Thresholds and ownership matter.

17
00:01:03.518 --> 00:01:16.206
A vulnerability finding becomes useful when the team knows which severity matters, which assets are critical, who owns remediation, what timeline is expected, and how exceptions are approved.

18
00:01:16.206 --> 00:01:23.323
An alert becomes useful when there is triage guidance, escalation criteria, and a way to document decisions.

19
00:01:23.323 --> 00:01:26.341
Monitoring without ownership creates noise.

20
00:01:26.341 --> 00:01:29.203
Monitoring with ownership creates action.

21
00:01:29.203 --> 00:01:33.381
Risk-based monitoring also means saying no to low-value noise.

22
00:01:33.381 --> 00:01:37.017
More alerts do not automatically mean better security.

23
00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:41.040
More dashboards do not automatically mean better awareness.

24
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:50.170
If a signal does not improve a decision, support evidence, trigger remediation, or inform risk, it should be tuned, summarized, or retired.

25
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:56.049
The best programs reduce noise so meaningful changes are easier to see and easier to act on.
